              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Do you think people will still read printed books in the future?",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A:",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I think they probably will, at least to some extent. Digital books are convenient, but many people still enjoy the feeling of holding a real book, and printed books don't need batteries. Having said that, I suspect the number of printed books will fall, especially in education, where tablets are cheaper in the long run. So printed books are unlikely to disappear completely, but they might become more of a luxury item.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Q:",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What would happen if public transport were free?",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Well, in that case, I imagine more people would leave their cars at home, which could reduce traffic and pollution. However, it depends on the quality of the service. If buses were free but slow and crowded, people probably wouldn't switch. Also, someone has to pay, so taxes might go up, which not everyone would accept.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
